### Page 1 of 21

```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:

Mayor Patrick Collins, and City Council
FROM:

TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager
DATE:

November 8, 2022
SUBJECT:
Professional Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Granite Peak
Environmental for Qualified Environmental Professional Services for an USEPA
Brownfield Assessment Grant
______________________________________________
One (1) Responsive Proposal was submitted under Request for Proposal (RFP) #2-23, for the
Qualified Environmental Professional Services for an USEPA Brownfield Assessment Grant
project.

The proposal was received from:
1. Granite Peak Environmental. Havre, Montana.

A proposal was also submitted by Ayers Associates, however their proposal did not contain the
required Federal Provisions as required by the terms of the Request for Proposal, therefore their
proposal has been rejected.

Upon review of the one (1) responsive proposal by the evaluation panel, the group has
recommended acceptance of the proposal submitted by Granite Peak Environmental, for a project
award amount of $488,760.00.

Basis for award was based on a Qualifications based review and scoring of proposals:  Granite
Peak Environmental, submitted the highest scoring proposal, therefore their sealed pricing
envelope was opened.

Funding:
025-21-2111-40-46509 (Federal Grants / U.S. Environmental Protection Agency)
```

### Page 2 of 21

```text
Planning and Development Office
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282
(Fax) 307-637-6366

MEMO
To:
Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and Members of the City Council
From:
Lonnie A Olson, Planner I
Subject: Professional Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Granite Peak
Environmental for Qualified Environmental Professional Services for an USEPA
Brownfield Assessment Grant
Date:
November 8, 2022

Background:

The item for consideration is a Professional Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and
Granite Peak Environmental for Qualified Environmental Professional Services for an USEPA
Brownfield Assessment Grant.

Staff anticipates this will build off the initial 2011 USEPA Assessment Grant that to date has resulted in
tens of millions of investments in the West Edge District. The second-tier brownfields missed the
funding cut during the initial grant however, the area is experiencing development interest and the likely
existence of contaminants is slowing property transactions. Assessment and area-wide planning
activities will be focused within the West Edge District of Cheyenne, the area stretches from Central
Avenue on the east to I-25 on the west, with the Union Pacific Railyard on the south and 24th Street on
the north.

The proposed Governing Body review schedule for this agreement is as follows:
•
Introduction and Referral: November 14, 2022
•
Finance Committee: November 21, 2022
•
Final Consideration: November 28, 2022

Staff Recommendation:

Staff recommends the Governing Body approve the agreement.

  Planning and Development Department
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282 (Fax) 307-637-6366
```

