```text
City of Cheyenne / Professional Services Agreement / RFP 2-23
Qualified Environmental Professional Services For An USEPA Brownfield Assessment Grant
Page 1 of 11
City Contract No. ____________

PROFESSIONAL SERVICES AGREEMENT
for
A QUALIFIED ENVIRONMENTAL PROFESSIONAL FOR
AN USEPA BROWNFIELD ASSESSMENT GRANT

This Professional Services Agreement (“Agreement”) is made and entered into by and between
the City of Cheyenne, located at 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001 (“City”),
and Granite Peak Environmental, located at P.O. Box 2344, Havre, Montana 59501
(“Consultant”).  This Agreement shall become effective upon the date of the last signature
affixed hereto.

RECITALS

In consideration of the mutual covenants and obligations herein expressed, it is agreed by and
between the parties as follows:

1.
SCOPE OF WORK
The Consultant agrees to provide services for Qualified Environmental Professional
Services for An USEPA Brownfield Assessment Grant, in accordance with City of
Cheyenne Request for Proposal (RFP) #2-23, incorporated herein by reference, and the
Consultant’s submitted proposal, incorporated herein by reference.

2.
TIME OF PERFORMANCE
The work included in this Scope of Work will be completed by September 30, 2025.

3.
COMPENSATION
In consideration of the services to be performed pursuant to this Agreement, the
Consultant will bill the City and the City agrees to pay Consultant a not to exceed amount
of Four Hundred Eighty-Eight Thousand, Seven Hundred Sixty Dollars
($488,760.00) as stated in Exhibit A – Price Proposal.

4.
CONSULTANT RESPONSIBILITY
In providing services under this Agreement, the Consultant shall perform in a manner
consistent with that degree of care and skill ordinarily exercised by members of the same
profession currently practicing under similar circumstances. Upon notice to the
Consultant, the Consultant will, without additional compensation, correct those services
not meeting such a standard.

5.
COMPLIANCE WITH LAWS
The Parties agree that they will perform their obligations as provided in this Agreement
in accordance with all applicable laws and ordinances.

By Stefanie Boster at 11:47 am, Nov 07, 2022
```

